  "h1": [
    "Dr. Jonathan Shadi"
  ],
  "word_count": 694,
  "body_markdown": "Skip to content\n\nCall or Text Us: (310) 954-9449\n\nRequest An Appointment\n\nPatient Registration\n\nHome\n\nAbout Us\n\nOur Team\n\nDr. Jonathan Shadi\n\nDr. Saman Vahedi\n\nOur Technology\n\nCone Beam 3D Imaging\n\nProcedures\n\nOral Surgery\n\nBone Grafting\n\nPre-Prosthetic Surgery\n\nPlatelet Rich Fibrin (PRF)\n\nOral Pathology\n\nOrthognathic (Corrective Jaw) Surgery\n\nDental Implants\n\nRestorative Dentistry\n\nFull Mouth Reconstruction\n\nImpacted Canines\n\nWisdom Teeth Removal\n\nEmergency Dentistry\n\nFacial Trauma Fractures\n\nSedation Dentistry\n\nPatient Center\n\nPatient Information\n\nInsurance & Finance\n\nAreas We Serve\n\nMar Vista\n\nPalms\n\nCulver City\n\nWestwood\n\nSawtelle\n\nCentury City\n\nBrentwood\n\nSanta Monica\n\nWest Los Angeles\n\nSurgical Instructions\n\nBefore Anesthesia\n\nOral Surgery Pre-Operative Instructions\n\nPost-Operative Instructions\n\nReferring Doctors\n\nBlogs\n\nContact Us\n\n\n# Dr. Jonathan Shadi\n\n\n\n### About Dr. Jonathan R. Shadi\n\n\n← Meet Our Team\n\nEducation\n\nB.S. Neuroscience\n\nUCLA, College Honors\n\nDental School\n\nDDS, USC School of Dentistry\n\nDean’s List • John Ingle Research Award 2009\n\nResidency\n\nOMFS Internship, VA Hospital Long Beach\n\nOMFS Residency, UCSF–Fresno, 2014\n\nClinical Focus\n\nDental Implants • Wisdom Teeth\n\nIV Anesthesia • Bone Grafting\n\nDr. Jonathan R. Shadi grew up in the West Los Angeles area, which makes Wilshire Oral Surgery and Implant Center more than a practice location for him. After earning his B.S. in Neuroscience from UCLA with College Honors, he attended the University of Southern California School of Dentistry, where he made the Dean’s List multiple times and received the John Ingle Research Award in 2009. That award recognized his contributions to dental research as a student, a distinction that reflects the analytical approach he brings to clinical work today.\n\nFollowing dental school, Dr. Shadi completed an Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery Internship at the Veterans’ Affairs Hospital in Long Beach before entering the full OMFS residency program at the University of California San Francisco–Fresno, completing in 2014. The UCSF–Fresno program trains surgeons across the full scope of oral and maxillofacial surgery, with significant exposure to trauma cases, reconstructive procedures, and complex anesthesia management. That training base is what qualifies Dr. Shadi to administer IV sedation and general anesthesia in-office, a capability that most general dental practices cannot offer.\n\nSince completing his residency, Dr. Shadi has practiced in the Greater Los Angeles area, returning to the Westside community where he spent his formative years. His clinical focus centers on single and complex dental implant surgery, wisdom teeth extractions, bone grafting and ridge augmentation, and IV general anesthesia. Patients whose cases involve significant bone loss, impaction, or the need for sedation will find that Dr. Shadi’s training makes him well suited to handle them without outside referrals.\n\nHis background in neuroscience gives Dr. Shadi a particular attentiveness to the anxiety and comfort concerns that accompany oral surgery for many patients. Procedures that involve sedation or surgical complexity are also procedures that require clear communication and unhurried pre-operative conversation. That is what patients consistently describe in their experience with Dr. Shadi at Wilshire Oral Surgery and Implant Center. You can also learn more about his colleague, Dr. Saman Vahedi, whose board certification and academic medical center residency training complement Dr. Shadi’s approach at the practice.\n\nRequest an Appointment → Meet Our Full Team\n\n\n### Contact Information\n\n\n12300 Wilshire Blvd #326 Los Angeles, CA 90025\n\n(310) 954-9449\n\n\n### Hours of Operation\n\n\nMonday\n\n8:00am – 4:00pm\n\nTuesday\n\nWednesday\n\nThursday\n\nFriday\n\nSaturday\n\nClosed\n\nSunday\n\n© 2026 Wilshire Oral Surgery and Implant Center. All Rights Reserved.\n\nAccessibility Statement\n\nMEET US\n\nSurgical Instructio...\n\nBlog\n\nMeet Us\n\nPatient Registration Form\n\nPre-prosthetic Surgery\n\nOral Surgery Pre-operative Instructions\n\nIV Sedation / General Anesthesia\n\nPost-operative Instructions",
